<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="faq"><div class="wrap narrow">
  <div class="sec-head"><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2></div>
  <details open><summary>Do they really help with the look of cellulite?<span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Yes. The raised knit gives your skin a constant micro-massage as you move, which helps smooth the look of dimples and loose skin over time. They don't cure cellulite (nothing does), but they soften how it looks, and the sculpting effect is visible the moment you put them on.</div></details>
  <details><summary>What exactly is 4D Compression?<span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ans">It is the everyday compression Japanese women wear under normal clothes, knit into a legging instead of a medical stocking. The 3D is the raised knit texture. The fourth D is the direction of the pressure: knit firmest at the ankle, easing up the thigh, the same way medical compression is engineered. Lookalikes are tightest at the waistband, which is upside down, and it is why they dig in while your legs still feel heavy. Pinch the fabric at the ankle, then at the thigh; you will feel the difference in ten seconds.</div></details>
  <details><summary>I lost a lot of weight and have loose skin. Will these help?<span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Honestly: nothing you wear tightens skin permanently. What these do is hold, shape and smooth the loose skin on your thighs while you wear them, so the shape you worked for shows now. Women who lost 50 to 100+ pounds tell us that is exactly what they wanted in the meantime.</div></details>
  <details><summary>I have lipedema or lymphedema. Are these for me?<span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ans">These are comfort-grade compression, not a medical device, and not a replacement for a garment your clinician prescribed. Many women keep their medical compression for flare days and want something easier and more normal-looking for everyday. That everyday pair is what we build. If you are under care, ask your clinician first.</div></details>
  <details><summary>Are they squat-proof? Will the waistband roll?<span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Fully opaque in a deep squat, in every color. The wide knit waistband holds without a thin elastic strip inside, so it stays put through sitting, driving and stairs, with no rolling and no digging.</div></details>
  <details><summary>What size should I order?<span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Use the "Check Your Size" tool in the buy box, or the chart; it is in inches and matches a real tape measure. Between two sizes? Size down for the firmer, held sculpt, size up for all-day softness.</div></details>
  <details><summary>The Amazon ones look identical and cost $25. Why not buy those?<span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ans">Read their reviews first: a printed-on texture that fades in the wash, and a waistband that rolls when you sit. The photos are copied from the ads; the legging is not. Ours is knit in zones with the pressure running ankle-up, and carries a 90-day guarantee a human actually honors.</div></details>
